      "informal_statement": "Given a measurable space $(\\Omega, m_0)$, a stochastic process $f \\colon \\mathbb{N} \\times \\Omega \\to E$, a filtration $\\mathcal{F}$ of sub-$\\sigma$-algebras of $m_0$ indexed by $\\mathbb{N}$, and a measure $\\mu$ on $\\Omega$, the martingale part of $f$ is defined as the process\n\\[\n\\text{martingalePart}(f, \\mathcal{F}, \\mu)(n) = f(n) - \\text{predictablePart}(f, \\mathcal{F}, \\mu)(n),\n\\]\nwhere $\\text{predictablePart}(f, \\mathcal{F}, \\mu)$ is the predictable part of $f$ as defined in the corresponding definition. This process is a martingale with respect to the filtration $\\mathcal{F}$ and measure $\\mu$."
