      "informal_statement": "Let $(\\Omega, m_0, \\mu)$ be a measure space with a filtration $\\mathcal{F}$ of sub-$\\sigma$-algebras of $m_0$ indexed by $\\mathbb{N}$, such that $\\mu$ is $\\sigma$-finite with respect to $\\mathcal{F}$. Given a stochastic process $f \\colon \\mathbb{N} \\times \\Omega \\to E$ that is adapted to $\\mathcal{F}$ and integrable (i.e., $f(n)$ is $\\mu$-integrable for all $n \\in \\mathbb{N}$), the martingale part $\\text{martingalePart}(f, \\mathcal{F}, \\mu)$ is a martingale with respect to $\\mathcal{F}$ and $\\mu$."
